      return `"Living here." They say it simply. "I had a house. It's gone. This wall is better than most walls in this part of the world."\nThey look at you without hostility.\n"Before that I worked the survey road — logistics, supply runs between the mine and the rail junction. I knew the route better than anyone."\nA pause.\n"When the company pulled out I had three days' notice." They look at the ruins around them.\n"This used to be a supply depot. Food stores, equipment, water. Good bones." They pat the wall. "I know where everything is."`;
    },
    options:['survivor_what_happened','survivor_railroad','survivor_bye'],
  },
  {
    id:'survivor_what_happened', label:"What happened to this place?",
    get text() {
      _survivorTalkSeen.add('survivor_settlement_known');
      return `"Altaverde pulled the rail. Without freight, the settlement couldn't sustain." They say it without bitterness, like a fact.\n"Forty people worked here. They all left inside a season."\nThey look at the broken walls.\n"The last ones out stripped the building for materials. I don't blame them." A pause.\n"I wasn't the last one out. I came back." They say it simply, without drama.\n"I know this ground. I know the water sources, the shelter points, where the dust devils don't go." They look at you.\n"There are worse places to be."`;
    },
    options:['survivor_railroad','survivor_leaving','survivor_bye'],
  },
  {
    id:'survivor_railroad', label:"The tracks — are those from the railroad?",
    get text() {
      _survivorTalkSeen.add('survivor_railroad_known');
      gainRep('badlands', 5);
      return `"Line seven. Ran east from Morrow Junction through the canyon settlements."\nThey gesture toward where the tracks would run.\n"They never pulled the rails. Just stopped running trains." A pause.\n"The metal was supposed to be valuable enough to reclaim. But the company dissolved the division before they could organize the salvage, and nobody else had the equipment to pull iron rails." They look toward the deep zone.\n"They're still there. Running into the rock. Connecting here to somewhere that doesn't exist anymore." They're quiet for a moment.\n"I walk the tracks sometimes. At night when the dust devils are quiet." They meet your eyes.\n"They run right past the mine entrance. The company mine. You can see where they put the spur track in for ore transport."`;
    },
    options:['survivor_what_happened','survivor_crane_question','survivor_bye'],
  },
  {
    id:'survivor_crane_question', label:"There's a man at the outpost. Crane.",
    get text() {
      _survivorTalkSeen.add('survivor_crane');
      return `They're quiet for a moment.\n"I know Crane." They say it carefully.\n"He came after the Collapse. Set up in the outpost." A pause.\n"He's watching something. I don't know if he knows that I know that." They look west.\n"The dust devils — he's been tracking them. Mapping where they go, how they move." They tilt their head.\n"He's thorough. Doesn't bother me." A longer pause.\n"Tell him the ones from the eastern vein are different from the canyon ones. He may already know. But tell him."`;
    },
    options:['survivor_what_happened','survivor_railroad','survivor_bye'],
